<p style="position:absolute;top:732px;left:109px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft04"><i>By:&#160;Teklay G. (AkU), Adane T. (MU), and Zelalem M.&#160;(HMU)&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;&#160;&#160; &#160;&#160;&#160; &#160; &#160;&#160;253&#160;</i></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:745px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft03">&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:83px;left:90px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft05">7.</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:82px;left:99px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft06">&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:83px;left:108px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft011">Write&#160;&#160;a&#160;&#160;categorical&#160;&#160;statement&#160;&#160;in&#160;&#160;which&#160;&#160;its&#160;&#160;subject&#160;&#160;class&#160;&#160;is&#160;&#160;entirely&#160;&#160;included&#160;&#160;in&#160;&#160;the&#160;<br/>predicate&#160;class.&#160;<br/>_________________________________________________________________&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:145px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft07"><b>I. Draw&#160;Venn&#160;diagrams&#160;for&#160;the&#160;following&#160;propositions.&#160;</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:170px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft011">1. &#160;Some rock-music&#160;lovers are&#160;not fans of Madonna.&#160;<br/>3.&#160;Some housing&#160;developments are&#160;complex&#160;that exclude children&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:216px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft07"><b>II. Use&#160;the&#160;modern&#160;square&#160;of&#160;opposition&#160;to determine&#160;whether&#160;the&#160;following&#160;immediate&#160;</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:232px;left:95px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft07"><b>inferences are&#160;valid&#160;or&#160;invalid&#160;from&#160;the&#160;Boolean&#160;standpoint</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:232px;left:397px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft05">.&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:258px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft011">&#160; &#160; &#160;1. Some country&#160;doctors are&#160;altruistic&#160;healers.&#160;<br/>Therefore, some&#160;country&#160;doctors are&#160;not&#160;altruistic&#160;healers.&#160;<br/>&#160; &#160; &#160;2.&#160;It is false that all weddings are&#160;light-hearted&#160;celebrations. Therefore, some weddings are&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:305px;left:104px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft05">not light-hearted celebrations.&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:331px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft012"><b>III. Convert&#160;the following propositions and&#160;state&#160;whether&#160;the&#160;converse&#160;is logically&#160;<br/>equivalent or&#160;not&#160;logically equivalent to the&#160;given proposition.&#160;</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:373px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft011">&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;&#160;a. All hurricanes are&#160;storms&#160;intensified by&#160;global warming.&#160;<br/>&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;&#160;b. No sex-change&#160;operations are&#160;completely&#160;successful procedures&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:419px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft07"><b>V</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:419px;left:81px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft05">.&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:419px;left:87px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft07"><b>Obvert the&#160;following&#160;propositions and&#160;state&#160;whether&#160;the&#160;obverse&#160;is logically equivalent&#160;</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:435px;left:95px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft07"><b>or&#160;not&#160;logically equivalent to the&#160;given proposition.&#160;</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:460px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft011">&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;a. All radically&#160;egalitarian societies are&#160;societies that do not&#160;preserve&#160;individual liberties.&#160;<br/>&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;b. No cult&#160;leaders&#160;are&#160;people who&#160;fail&#160;to brainwash their followers.&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:507px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft08"><b>References&#160;&#160;</b></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:539px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft09"><i><b>Textbooks&#160;</b></i></p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:576px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft010">Hurley, Patrick&#160;J.&#160;(2014)&#160;A&#160;Concise Introduction to Logic,&#160;12th Edition,&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:575px;left:393px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft05">Wadsworth, Cengage&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;</p>
<p style="position:absolute;top:596px;left:72px;white-space:nowrap" class="ft05">&#160;</p>
